# Out of scope for v1

Do **not** add, scaffold, or "future-proof" for any of the following without an explicit
ADR overriding this rule:

- Dialogue and lip-sync
- Durations other than exactly 40 seconds (4 × 10s beats)
- User-supplied reference characters
- Voiceover
- An editing timeline / manual re-ordering UI
- Resolution above 1080p

If a request implies one of these (e.g. "add a voiceover track option"), say that it's
out of scope for v1 per the PRD and ask whether the person wants to open an ADR to change
that, rather than quietly implementing it.
